[Id "queens-gambit"]
[Name "Queen's Gambit"]
[Side "white"]
[ECO "D06-D69"]
[Description "1.d4 d5 2.c4: offer a wing pawn to win the centre."]
[Tags "positional, solid"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 {c4 attacks d5; if Black takes, White wins it back and owns the centre.} 2... e6 {@variation Declined}
  (2... dxc4 {@variation Accepted} 3. Nf3 {Nf3 develops first and stops …e5.} 3... Nf6 4. e3 e6 5. Bxc4 {Bxc4 wins the pawn back with a lead in development.} 5... c5
    (5... Be7 6. O-O {O-O: develop quickly; Nc3, Qe2 and e4 come next.}
{@line id=queens-gambit-accepted-be7 level=2 tier=side name="5…Be7" summary="Against the quiet …Be7, just castle and develop; aim for e4."}
)
  6. O-O a6 7. a4 {a4 stops …b5, which would gain space with tempo on the bishop.}
{@line id=queens-gambit-accepted level=1 tier=main name="Accepted (2…dxc4)" summary="Don't rush to win the pawn back: develop, retake on c4, and stop …b5 with a4."}
7... Nc6 8. Qe2 {Qe2 connects the rooks and supports a later d5 push.} 8... cxd4 9. Rd1 {Rd1 puts the rook opposite the d4 pawn before taking it back.} 9... Be7 10. exd4 {exd4 leaves White an isolated d-pawn, but with active pieces and d5 ideas.}
{@line id=queens-gambit-accepted-deep level=2 tier=main name="7.a4 Nc6" summary="White gets an isolated d-pawn with active pieces: aim for the d5 push."}
)
  (2... c6 {@variation Slav} 3. cxd5 {cxd5 makes a symmetrical structure where White keeps the extra move.} 3... cxd5 4. Nc3 Nf6 5. Bf4 {Bf4 develops actively before e3.} 5... Nc6 6. e3 Bf5
    (6... a6 7. Bd3 {Bd3 develops and stops …Bf5.} (7. Qb3 {@alt})
{@line id=queens-gambit-slav-a6 level=2 tier=side name="Exchange: 6…a6" summary="Against …a6, develop the bishop to d3 first so …Bf5 is no longer possible."}
)
  7. Nf3 e6 8. Bb5 {Bb5 pins the c6 knight, adding pressure on Black's centre.} (8. Qb3 {@alt})
{@line id=queens-gambit-slav-exchange level=1 tier=main name="Exchange (3.cxd5)" summary="Against the Slav, trade on d5, develop fast and use the extra move: Bf4, e3, Nf3, Bb5."}
)
  (2... Nf6 {@variation 2…Nf6} 3. cxd5 {cxd5 wins space: Black can't keep a pawn on d5.} 3... Nxd5 4. Nf3 {Nf3 develops; e4 next builds a big centre.}
{@line id=queens-gambit-2nf6 level=1 tier=side name="2…Nf6" summary="Against 2…Nf6, take on d5 and develop; Black has given up the centre."}
)
  (2... e5 {@variation Albin Countergambit} 3. dxe5 {dxe5 takes the pawn; the d4 pawn will be a target later.} 3... d4 4. Nf3 {Nf3 defends e5 and avoids the trap after 4.e3? Bb4+.} 4... Nc6 5. g3 {g3 prepares Bg2, aiming the bishop at the queenside.} 5... Bg4 6. Bg2 {Bg2 develops and eyes b7; the d4 pawn will need a lot of defending.}
{@line id=queens-gambit-albin level=1 tier=side name="Albin Countergambit (2…e5)" summary="Take the Albin pawn, develop with Nf3, g3 and Bg2, and keep the e5 pawn protected."}
)
3. Nc3 Nf6 4. cxd5 {cxd5 fixes Black's pawns and gives White a clear plan.} 4... exd5
  (4... Nxd5 5. e4 {e4 grabs the centre with tempo on the d5 knight.} 5... Nxc3 6. bxc3 {bxc3 gives White a big pawn centre.}
{@line id=queens-gambit-qgd-nxd5 level=2 tier=side name="4…Nxd5" summary="If Black takes back with the knight, push e4 at once and build a big centre."}
)
5. Bg5 {Bg5 pins the f6 knight, the main defender of d5.} 5... Be7
  (5... c6 6. e3 Be7 7. Bd3 Nbd7 8. Qc2 {Qc2 stops …Bf5, which would trade Black's problem bishop.}
{@line id=queens-gambit-qgd-c6 level=1 tier=main name="Exchange: 5…c6" summary="Trade on d5, pin with Bg5, then Bd3 and Qc2 to keep Black's light-squared bishop passive."}
8... O-O 9. Nf3 {Nf3 develops and watches e5.} 9... Re8 10. O-O {O-O completes development; now the queenside plan starts.} 10... Nf8 11. Rab1 {Rab1 prepares b4-b5, the minority attack against Black's c6 pawn.}
{@line id=queens-gambit-qgd-minority level=2 tier=main name="Exchange, minority attack" summary="The minority attack: Rab1, b4, b5, and trade on c6 to leave Black a weak pawn."}
)
6. e3 {e3 supports d4 and frees the f1 bishop.} 6... O-O 7. Bd3 {Bd3 develops towards Black's king and stops …Bf5.}
{@line id=queens-gambit-qgd-exchange level=1 tier=main name="Exchange (4.cxd5)" summary="Trade on d5, pin with Bg5, then e3 and Bd3: a clear plan for White."}
7... c6
  (7... h6 8. Bh4 {Bh4 keeps the pin on the f6 knight.} 8... c6 9. Qc2 {Qc2 stops …Bf5 and lines up on h7.}
{@line id=queens-gambit-qgd-h6 level=2 tier=main name="Exchange: 7…h6" summary="Against …h6, keep the pin with Bh4, then Qc2 as usual."}
)
8. Qc2 {Qc2 stops …Bf5, which would trade Black's problem bishop.}
{@line id=queens-gambit-qgd-be7-c6 level=2 tier=main name="Exchange: 7…c6" summary="Against …c6, Qc2 stops …Bf5; then Nf3 (or Nge2), castle and start the minority attack."} *
